WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.630
Type eight to the power two
thirds into a calculator.

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:04.760
Out comes four.

3
00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:06.450
Exactly four.

4
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:09.540
Now try twenty-seven to
the power two thirds.

5
00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:11.110
Exactly nine.

6
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:14.570
A fraction as a power, and
a whole number comes out.

7
00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:16.040
How can that happen?

8
00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:19.430
Is the calculator just
multiplying eight by two thirds?

9
00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:21.260
Or is something else going on?

10
00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:24.210
In this mission, you'll
use the laws of indices,

11
00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:28.560
for multiplying, dividing and
raising powers of the same base.

12
00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:32.060
You'll meet zero, negative
and fractional indices.

13
00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:34.730
And you'll keep answers exact with surds,

14
00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:37.070
and rationalise denominators.

15
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:42.140
Your mission: work out why eight to the
power two thirds comes out as exactly

16
00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:42.840
four.
